{"p4": {"friction": "The rubric has no relation for an introduction theorem that restates a later result (\"Theorem 1.1 (Corollary 5.2)\"), so equivalent-to, generalises and depends-on all fit poorly. A proposition saying \"this construction defines a contravariant functor\" (Proposition 4.7) uses the word 'defines' inside a proven result.", "doubt": "Claim 6: whether a parenthetical result label counts as an identity assertion. Claim 5: whether a proposition's 'defines a functor' is a defines or a proves. Claims 3 and 7: whether a definition tagged with a citation (\"[7, Definitions 8.5]\") must be cited even when the paper restates it as its own; I followed the rubric's Definition 1.6 [Sch19] example.", "missing_context": "The section and proof text are missing; the input holds only the abstract, the introduction and the result statements, so depends-on or locator subtleties inside proofs could not be checked.", "proposed_change": "Add to the rubric: 'An introduction result labelled with a later result (\"Theorem 1.1 (Corollary 5.2)\") is a restatement. Grade claims relating the two as wrong-relation unless the paper asserts their equivalence.' Also add: 'A Definition carrying an inline citation is cited modality.'", "process_observation": "Two claims in this paper (2 and 10) are near-duplicates of the same Corollary 5.2(2) assertion. The extractor also put objects (Spec(...), a functor) in the proves subject slot twice."}}
